# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Every service image builds with the repo root as its context (see the
# `context: ..` entries in infra/docker-compose.yml), because the Dockerfiles
# COPY workspace manifests and packages/. Without this file that context is
# ~2.4GB — dominated by the two Python virtualenvs at 1.2GB each — and the
# daemon transfers all of it, once per image, before the first RUN executes.
# Eight images made `docker compose up --build` slow enough to look hung.
#
# Correctness matters here as much as speed. node_modules and .venv are built
# for the host platform; copying them into a Linux image shadows what
# `npm ci` / `pip install` produce inside it, so a native module compiled for
# Windows silently wins over the correct Linux build.
# =============================================================================

# Dependency trees — reinstalled inside the image for the target platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info

# Build output — regenerated by the image's own build stage.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and IDE state.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.antigravity-ide
.idea
.vscode

# Caches.
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.npm
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets must never enter an image layer. .env is gitignored, but the build
# context is not git — without this line `COPY . .` in any future Dockerfile
# would bake the Supabase password and JWT_SECRET into a distributable image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
infra/k8s/overlays/local/01-secrets.yaml

# NOT excluded: infra/certs/. It holds the pinned Supabase root CA, which is a
# public certificate, not a secret — and packages/config/src/db.ts reads it at
# runtime and *throws* when a .supabase.co connection string needs it and it is
# absent, rather than silently downgrading to an unverified TLS session. An
# image built against a Supabase DATABASE_URL without it fails to start.

# Runtime artifacts written by a previous local run.
storage_fallback
**/storage_fallback

# Documentation and planning material — no service reads these at runtime.
docs
conductor
.agents
*.md
!README.md

# Local tooling output.
docs/benchmarks/*.json
scratchpad
